main.py

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §3/A (is & small-int interning). PLR: two separate
int("100000") objects are distinct (100000 is not a cached small int),
so x is not y holds. CBMC models `is not` as value inequality with no
identity model, so it computes False and the assertion fails. This
KNOWNBUG regex states the PLR-correct SUCCESSFUL that the value model
cannot produce. Faithful modeling would require boxing ints with
identity, which the value-based model does not do.
